<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Ried</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-sixth-coalition">War of the Sixth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Ried was signed on 8 October 1813 at Ried im Innkreis between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Bavaria left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, in return for a guarantee of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> and of compensation for any lands it had to return to Austria. It allowed Bavaria to keep its kingdom and most of its Napoleonic gains.</p></div>
